course: dictionary
lesson: 3416
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Long exposure to loud sound can damage hearing without any pain.» Here exposure means being near something harmful for a long time.
explain: «Exposure is how much light a photo lets in, and focus is which part looks sharp.» In this sentence exposure is about light in a photo, not about being outside in the cold. The words photo and light are the clues.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Does «being near something harmful for a long time» make sense with the loud sound? Yes, so it is the right meaning. If it does not fit, try another meaning from the dictionary.
fact: Exposure can mean being out in cold, wind or weather without protection, which can make you very ill.
fact: «Exposure to» something means being near it or affected by it, such as «exposure to the sun» or «exposure to germs».
fact: Exposure can also mean making something hidden known to the public.
fact: In photography, exposure is the amount of light let in for one picture.
fact: The oldest surviving camera photograph needed hours or even days of exposure, so the camera had to be still for a very long time.
exercise: «Long exposure to loud sound can damage hearing without any pain.» What does exposure mean here? | Showing a secret to the public | Taking a picture with a camera | *Being near something harmful for a long time | Being out in the cold without a coat
exercise: «Exposure is how much light a photo lets in.» What does exposure mean in this sentence? | A kind of food | Being out in cold weather | *The amount of light let in for one picture | Making a secret known
exercise: Which phrase means being out in cold weather without protection? | sun exposure, meaning light from the sky | die of exposure | *die of exposure, meaning it is the cold and weather that cause harm | media exposure, meaning news on the screen
test: «The news report gave the hidden scandal media exposure.» What does exposure mean here? | A safe place to hide | The amount of light in a photo | *Making something hidden known to the public | Being out in the rain
test: «Wrap up warm, because long exposure to cold wind can make you ill.» What does exposure mean? | Making a secret known | Taking a photo with a long time for the light | *Being out in cold weather without protection | Hiding from the sun
exam: «The camera needed a longer exposure in the dark.» What does exposure mean? | Making a secret public | *The amount of light let in for one picture | Being out in the cold | Being near something harmful
